# Hash-locked tooling for the packaging E2E CI job.
# Regenerate: uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes --strip-extras \
#   --python-version 3.10 --output-file=requirements-packaging.lock requirements-packaging.in
#
# The packaging-e2e and e2e-installed jobs install this lock into the same
# environment as requirements-ci.txt. The two locks share packages that neither
# input names (idna, packaging, importlib-metadata, tomli, zipp), and
# scripts/lock_conflict_ratchet.py fails the build when they disagree. They
# agreed only as long as nobody regenerated one of them alone: the first
# Dependabot bump that moved idna in the CI lock left this one behind (#544).
# The constraint makes this lock follow the CI lock; the relock workflow
# compiles the CI lock first because of it.
-c requirements-ci.txt

build==1.6.1
twine==7.0.0
check-wheel-contents==0.6.3
